        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li dir=\"ltr\">[... when she is (still) under] his jurisdiction a division will be made of the land and what\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">and what remains of her dowry into two equal portions. Half her husband will acquire,\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">and half will return to the house of her fathers. And it is a monetary stipulation (and) is valid. And\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Man\u1e63\u016br, this groom, acknowledged that he received in full all th[at] is written and specified\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">above. And he said: \"I am obligated to make payment, whether myself or from my heirs who will stand after me.\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">And all things that I possess and that I shall acquire, whether real estate or movables</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">will be surety and guarantees for the payment of this marriage contract.\u201d And they stipulated between themselves con-</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">-cerning hate and love and life and death and all the court stipulations from beginning</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">to end. And they also stipulated between themselves that \u1e24a\u1e93iyya would live in Tyre twelve\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">months, and afterwards he will move her to the city of Akko, without delaying or deferring.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Further they stipulated between themselves: If m(aster) Nathan, her father, should happen to go to Akko, after</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">his daughter \u1e24a\u1e93iyya goes (there), he will live in this house, whether he is alone or his wife\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">is with him and his children, whether to visit or to dwell (there) all his life, because on this condition he had given it to his daughter</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">\u1e24a\u1e93iyya; and he had imposed on her this stipulation. Man\u1e63\u016br, her husband, obligated himself by it without (any) protest\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">and without hesitating. And the two sides took upon themselves the security and stringency of this\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">deed according to the strength and stringency of all valid deeds, verified in court</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">not like promises nor like formularies of documents. And with this understanding, the two sides concluded\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">and consented, not being coerced nor compelled; and they told the scribe\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">to write and the witnesses to testify. And we performed with them a complete, strict qinyan,\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">with an implement fit for doing this, for all that is written and specified above. Valid,\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">correct, and verified is this marriage contract wherever produced and read, whether\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">according to the statutes of our lords the sages or according to the laws of the gentiles. May he build and prosper. In good order.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">The papers are three. There is written on the joint, perpendicularly, in two places \"true and corr[ect].\"</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">And the number of lines is ninety-four. Strong and firm.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">\"I have read this copy and have transcribed the testimony which is in the ketubba. And it is\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">correct,\u201d written by Joseph ha-Levi b. R. Manasseh (who) r(ests in) E(den).\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Mevorakh b. Menahem (whose) s(oul is at) r(est).</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Samuel b. R. Moses he-\u1e25aver (who) r(ests in) E(den).\u00a0 </li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
